    <!--Note: Font families can easily be broken by the metadata on the font file.
    If the typeface name does not match what is specified here EXACTLY, then the font
    will fail to load without any error messages.
    
    Use FontForge (https://fontforge.org/en-US/) to inspect and edit this meta data.
    
    The typeface in FontForge is listed as FamilyName in FontForge.
       FontForge >> Element >> PS Names >> FamilyName.
    
    Preferred Family will also break the Typeface lookup. So delete that if it exists.
       FontForge >> Element >> TTF Names >> Preferred Family
    
    - Jarryd, 15-NOV-23-->
    
    
    
    <!--Note: Many of the fonts done before RLL1 (2025) are done individually, with 
    a new font family for every single font variation - eg. new <FontFamily> for Barlow Reg,
    Barlow Bold, Barlow Italic, etc. THIS IS UNNEEDED.
    
    If Exo 2 Bold, Exo 2 Italic, Exo 2 SemiBold etc are all under the Family Name "Exo 2" in the
    metadata, this will work correctly if we put the font file path as  "../Fonts/#Exo 2"
    because they are all under the umbrella of Exo 2. To get Bold Italic, we would then use 
    the SubFamily and the various weight class and style metadata properties:
    
           FontForge >> Element >> Font Info >> PS Names >> Weight              == matches up to FontWeight
           FontForge >> Element >> Font Info >> OS/2 >> Weight Class            == matches up to FontWeight
           FontForge >> Element >> Font Info >> OS/2 >> Style Map               == matches up to FontWeight & FontStyle
           FontForge >> Element >> Font Info >> TTF Names >> Styles (SubFamily) == matches up to FontWeight & FontStyle
    
        Note Again:  all I know is that it works if I set all these. dunno if they're ALL needed though,
        and testing that is a problem for another day
    
    All the files still need to be added into paNoesisFontProvider.cpp, but the <FontFamily> 
    itself can group all of these files into one if done correctly, making this file significantly
    shorter and using the styles a lot easier. 
    
    - El, 3/3/2025 -->



    <FontFamily x:Key="Exo2">
        <!-- Latin based            -->
        ../Fonts/#Exo 2,
        <!-- Fallback               -->
        ../Fonts/NotoSansCJKjp-Regular.otf#Noto Sans CJK JP,
    </FontFamily>  

    <FontFamily x:Key="Ranade">
        <!-- Latin based            -->
        ../Fonts/#Ranade,
        <!-- Fallback               -->
        ../Fonts/NotoSansCJKjp-Regular.otf#Noto Sans CJK JP,
